BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club
UID:event_317341246@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T064705Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261123T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261123T110000
SUMMARY:Mountains-to-Sea Trail Highway 25 toward Bent Creek
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club 2.0\nThis is a fa
 irly easy hike\, and we go at a high average to low advanced speed\, which
  is roughly about 3.0 to 3.2 mph. There are no super long hills. It's pret
 ty undulating all the way.\n\nWell behaved dogs on leashes are welcome to 
 attend.\n\nWhen you arrive\, park at the gravel lot across from the trail 
 head. You'll see some people gathering by their cars. I've recently correc
 ted the PIN setting on the map\, so it should be correct. Here are some di
 rections to use too: When going south on Hendersonville Road\, go past Car
 olina Day School and turn right at the Blue Ridge Parkway exit. When you g
 et to the parkway turn RIGHT. You will see parking on the left and right s
 ide of the road. Park there.\n\nMountains-to-Sea-Trail hikes are designed 
 for fitness and community among people who are already reasonably fit. It'
 s not an endurance hike by any means\, but it is designed so we can get ou
 r hearts beating a bit while still being able to have a conversation and m
 eet new people.\nWhen you arrive\, we'll circle up and introduce ourselves
  briefly. There will be a person who is a sweep. This person is the person
  who walks last and makes sure no one gets lost.\n\nWe leave the parking s
 pot at 9:10. If someone needs a nature break\, we wait fo you\, but it's n
 ot a hike where we stop and take photos or frequent breaks. We basically k
 eep hiking until the 1/2 way mark\, then turn around after a short (approx
 imately 5 minute) break. Then we keep that same pace on the way back. If w
 e get on a trail right at 9:10\, we are normally finished around 10:50.\n\
 nThese are out and back hikes\, meaning that we hike in and turn around ha
 lf way to return back.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-mountains-to-sea-trail-hiki
 ng-club/events/317341246/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261108T161702Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261108T161702Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club
UID:event_317507361@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T064705Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261130T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261130T110000
SUMMARY:Craven Gap
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club 2.0\nThis is a fa
 irly undulating hike. It's narrow at first with some rocky steps and then 
 narrow and rooty for most of the way until halfway when there's a short cl
 imb to the 2.5 mile mark. We go about 2.7 to 2.9 mph.\n\nWell behaved dogs
  on leashes are welcome to attend.\n\nWhen you arrive\, park at the gravel
  lot on the other side of the road\, closest to Town Mountain. You'll see 
 some people gathering by their cars.\n\nMountains-to-Sea-Trail hikes are d
 esigned for fitness and community among people who are already reasonably 
 fit. It's not an endurance hike by any means\, but it is designed so we ca
 n get our hearts beating a bit while still being able to have a conversati
 on and meet new people.\nWhen you arrive\, we'll circle up and introduce o
 urselves briefly. There will be a person who is a sweep. This person is th
 e person who walks last and makes sure no one gets lost.\n\nWe leave the p
 arking spot at 9:10. If someone needs a nature break\, we wait fo you\, bu
 t it's not a hike where we stop and take photos or frequent breaks. We bas
 ically keep hiking until the 1/2 way mark\, then turn around after a short
  (approximately 5 minute) break. Then we keep that same pace on the way ba
 ck. If we get on a trail right at 9:10\, we are normally finished around 1
 0:50.\n\nThese are out and back hikes\, meaning that we hike in and turn a
 round half way to return back.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-mountains-to-sea-trail-hiki
 ng-club/events/317507361/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261120T005443Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261120T005443Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club
UID:event_317507367@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T064705Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261204T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261204T110000
SUMMARY:Rattlesnake Lodge Hike
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club 2.0\nMeet at the 
 Ox Creek Trailhead at 9 a.m. We tend to park at the 2nd and third turn off
 \, once you turn left onto Ox Creek from the Parkway.\n\nWe'll leave for t
 he hike at 9:10 a.m. This hike is very rocky\, so it's hard on the footing
 . Most of the hike to the ruins of the lodge is a slight upgrade and\, on 
 the return\, there is a long stretch of incline just before the hike ends.
  When it's wet it can be slippery.\n\nMountains-to-Sea-Trail hikes are des
 igned for fitness and community among already experienced hikers. We repea
 t the same trails weekly so that\, over time\, we enjoy the beauty of each
  trail. We limit our hikes to two hours because many of us work and have t
 o be somewhere else by 11:15 or so. Thus\, it's not possible to wait for s
 lower hikers. We shuttle\, so if someone is slower\, the group would have 
 to wait in order to give a ride back to the starting point. Thus\, the nee
 d to be on the same page with regard to hiking pace.\n\nHikers who are new
  to hiking will likely be more comfortable on another meet up hike designe
 d for people who are just beginning hiking or trying to get into shape for
  hiking. You might consider "WNC Easy Hikers Group\," for instance.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-mountains-to-sea-trail-hiki
 ng-club/events/317507367/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261120T005547Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261120T005547Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
